TITLE:: PltVector
summary:: Vectorscope: one channel against the other
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltWave, Classes/PltMeter

DESCRIPTION::
Stereo width, phase and mono compatibility, made visible.

A vertical line means the two channels are identical, a horizontal line means they
are opposite in phase, a circle means they are unrelated. The diagonals are the mid
and side axes, so a cloud leaning along one of them is leaning toward mono or toward
difference. The correlation in the caption says the same as a number.

Older frames are kept and drawn fainter, which is what makes a moving image readable
rather than a flicker.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Two collections of samples.
argument:: left
argument:: right
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: live
Live, from two adjacent busses through a looping link::Classes/RecordBuf::.
argument:: bus
argument:: server
argument:: frames
Samples held per frame.
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: fromSoundFile
The first two channels of a file, decimated to code::maxFrames::. A mono file plots
against itself, which is the diagonal.

METHOD:: correlation
Correlation of two channels: 1 identical, 0 unrelated, -1 inverted. Computed about
zero rather than about the mean, because a DC offset is a fault in audio and should
not be quietly removed from the reading.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: pushFrame
One frame of two channels.
METHOD:: correlation
METHOD:: start
METHOD:: stop
METHOD:: persistence
How many past frames are kept.
METHOD:: alpha
METHOD:: dotSize
METHOD:: pollRate
METHOD:: dotColorKey
METHOD:: guideColorKey
METHOD:: xs
METHOD:: ys
METHOD:: trails

EXAMPLES::
code::
// live
s.boot;
v = PltVector.live(0).front;
x = { var m = PinkNoise.ar(0.2); [m + BrownNoise.ar(0.05), m + BrownNoise.ar(0.05)] }.play;
v.correlation;
x.free;
x = { PinkNoise.ar(0.2) ! 2 }.play;      // identical: a vertical line
x.free; v.close;

// a file
PltVector.fromSoundFile("~/sound.wav".standardizePath).front;

// data only
(
var n = 2000;
var a = Array.fill(n, { |i| sin(i * 0.05) });
PltVector.correlation(a, a.neg);         // -1
)
::
